# Build context = monorepo root for all images (ant-cli, ant-ui, ant-cli IDE).
# Docker resolves this single .dockerignore relative to that context, so it
# applies to every image build. Keep it conservative: only exclude paths that
# are reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image or must never enter it (secrets, VCS).

# --- Version control ---
.git
.gitignore

# --- Dependencies (reinstalled via `pnpm install` in every stage) ---
**/node_modules

# --- Build outputs (recompiled inside the builder stage) ---
**/dist
**/.vite
**/coverage

# --- Tests (no image build step runs them; runtime images copy only src/) ---
**/tests

# --- Secrets: mirror .gitignore's secret rules ---
# Excludes packages/ant-cli/.env (real backend secrets) and *.local overrides,
# while KEEPING the committed public build config that the ant-ui/ant-site Vite
# builds depend on (.env.development / .env.production / .env.example.*).
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.env.backup
**/.env.bak
env (*)
# Keep the committed example (mirrors .gitignore's `!.env.example.local`).
!**/.env.example.local

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
**/*.log
.claude
.cursor
